Repair the following CommonJS module. Return a corrected complete source file exporting exactly `{ selectPage }`.

`selectPage(route, pages)` must require a string route and a non-null, non-array object whose values are strings. It removes every leading and trailing slash from the route while preserving internal slashes, then returns the matching own-property value or `null`. Empty normalized routes are valid keys. It must not mutate either argument.

Known-bad source:
```javascript
function selectPage(route, pages) {
  if (typeof route !== 'string') throw new TypeError('route must be a string');
  if (!pages || typeof pages !== 'object' || Array.isArray(pages)) throw new TypeError('pages must be an object');
  for (const value of Object.values(pages)) {
    if (typeof value !== 'string') throw new TypeError('page values must be strings');
  }
  const normalized = route.replace(/^\/|\/$/, '');
  return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(pages, normalized) ? pages[normalized] : null;
}

module.exports = { selectPage };
```

